{"id":"uk_vibration_data","title":"Bearing frequency data are included in this catalogue for two","source":"UK_vibration_data.pdf","theme":"roulements","pages":[{"pageNumber":1,"blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Bearing frequency data are included in this catalogue for two purposes:"},{"type":"text","text":"Part Frequencies (per shaft rev.) Roller details"},{"type":"text","text":"Shaft Diameter d"},{"type":"text","text":"Bearing Reference"},{"type":"text","text":"Cage Roller Outer Inner PCD (mm) No. Diameter (mm)"},{"type":"text","text":"- to allow machine designers to check excitation frequencies against resonant frequencies in the machine, - to allow correct input into condition monitoring equipment that uses this data."},{"type":"text","text":"35 01 B 35M 0.405 2.538 4.051 5.949 62.71 10 11.91"},{"type":"text","text":"40 01 B 40M 0.405 2.538 4.051 5.949 62.71 10 11.91"},{"type":"text","text":"45 01E B 45M 0.415 2.857 4.980 7.020 76.50 12 13.00"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Bearing Geometry and Frequencies of Bearing Parts"},{"type":"text","text":"50 01E B 50M 0.415 2.857 4.980 7.020 76.50 12 13.00 02 B 50M 0.402 2.452 4.020 5.980 80.96 10 15.88"},{"type":"text","text":"A roller bearing will excite vibrations at certain frequencies related to the number, size and pitch circle diameter of the rollers. To some extent this excitation is present even with new bearings in perfect condition, as the load is carried on discrete, elastic, rolling elements which are constantly changing in angular position."},{"type":"text","text":"55 01E B 55M 0.417 2.934 5.840 8.160 90.50 14 15.00"},{"type":"text","text":"60 01E B 60M 0.417 2.934 5.840 8.160 90.50 14 15.00 02 B 60M 0.411 2.730 4.936 7.064 98.43 12 17.46"},{"type":"text","text":"65 01E B 65M 0.417 2.934 5.840 8.160 90.50 14 15.00 02 B 65M 0.411 2.730 4.936 7.064 98.43 12 17.46"},{"type":"text","text":"The tables opposite and on the following pages indicate the frequencies of bearing parts per shaft revolution, which can be used to calculate excitation frequencies directly by multiplying the tabulated frequencies by the shaft speed."},{"type":"text","text":"70 01E B 70M 0.420 3.053 5.883 8.117 106.50 14 17.00 02 B 70M 0.411 2.719 4.932 7.068 115.89 12 20.64"},{"type":"text","text":"75 100 B 75M 0.448 4.723 8.953 11.047 95.50 20 10.00 01E B 75M 0.420 3.053 5.883 8.117 106.50 14 17.00 02 B 75M 0.411 2.719 4.932 7.068 115.89 12 20.64"},{"type":"text","text":"The frequencies listed are explained as follows:"},{"type":"text","text":"‘Cage’ – the frequency at which a point on the cage enters and leaves the loaded zone of the bearing."},{"type":"text","text":"80 01E B 80M 0.423 3.187 6.774 9.226 124.00 16 19.00 02 B 80M 0.417 2.917 5.833 8.167 133.35 14 22.23"},{"type":"text","text":"‘Roller’ – the frequency at which a point on a given roller passes into contact with either the inner or outer race."},{"type":"text","text":"85 100 B 85M 0.446 4.592 8.924 11.076 111.50 20 12.00 01E B 85M 0.423 3.187 6.774 9.226 124.00 16 19.00 02 B 85M 0.417 2.917 5.833 8.167 133.35 14 22.23"},{"type":"text","text":"‘Outer’ – the frequency at which a point on the outer race comes into contact with successive rollers."},{"type":"text","text":"90 01E B 90M 0.423 3.187 6.774 9.226 124.00 16 19.00 02 B 90M 0.417 2.917 5.833 8.167 133.35 14 22.23"},{"type":"text","text":"‘Inner’ – the frequency at which a point on the inner race comes into contact with successive rollers."},{"type":"text","text":"95 01E B 95M 0.422 3.138 6.756 9.244 141.50 16 22.00"},{"type":"text","text":"100 B 100M 0.446 4.553 8.915 11.085 129.00 20 14.00 01E B 100M 0.422 3.138 6.756 9.244 141.50 16 22.00 02 B 100M 0.417 2.917 5.833 8.167 152.40 14 25.40 03 B 100M 0.384 2.038 3.839 6.161 177.80 10 41.28"},{"type":"text","text":"The tables also list the pitch circle diameters and number of rollers, for use with condition monitoring equipment that accepts this information."},{"type":"text","text":"100"},{"type":"text","text":"Note that the contact angle is 0 in all cases."},{"type":"text","text":"105 01E B 105M 0.422 3.138 6.756 9.244 141.50 16 22.00 02 B 105M 0.417 2.917 5.833 8.167 152.40 14 25.40"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Vibration levels"},{"type":"text","text":"100 B 110M 0.442 4.251 8.840 11.160 146.50 20 17.00 01 B 110M 0.430 3.501 6.880 9.120 158.75 16 22.23 02 B 110M 0.417 2.917 5.833 8.167 171.45 14 28.58 03 B 110M 0.392 2.199 3.917 6.083 190.50 10 41.28"},{"type":"text","text":"Velocity readings for a properly installed new bearing may be as high as 4mm/second."},{"type":"text","text":"110"},{"type":"text","text":"Typically, alarm levels should be set no higher than 15mm/ second."},{"type":"text","text":"115 01 B 115M 0.430 3.501 6.880 9.120 158.75 16 22.23 02 B 115M 0.417 2.917 5.833 8.167 171.45 14 28.58"},{"type":"text","text":"Shutdown level should be set no higher than 20mm/second."},{"type":"image","src":"/docs/img/uk_vibration_data/p000_img00.png","caption":"Figure — page 1"},{"type":"table","headers":["Shaft\nDiameter\nd","Bearing\nReference","Part Frequencies (per shaft rev.)","","","","Roller details","",""],"rows":[["","","Cage","Roller","Outer","Inner","PCD\n(mm)","No.","Diameter\n(mm)"],["35","01 B 35M","0.405","2.538","4.051","5.949","62.71","10","11.91"]]},{"type":"table","headers":["40","","01 B 40M","0.405","2.538","4.051","5.949","62.71","10","11.91"],"rows":[["45","","01E B 45M","0.415","2.857","4.980","7.020","76.50","12","13.00"]]},{"type":"table","headers":["50","","01E B 50M","0.415","2.857","4.980","7.020","76.50","12","13.00"],"rows":[["","","02 B 50M","0.402","2.452","4.020","5.980","80.96","10","15.88"],["55","","01E B 55M","0.417","2.934","5.840","8.160","90.50","14","15.00"]]},{"type":"table","headers":["60","","01E B 60M","0.417","2.934","5.840","8.160","90.50","14","15.00"],"rows":[["","","02 B 60M","0.411","2.730","4.936","7.064","98.43","12","17.46"],["65","","01E B 65M","0.417","2.934","5.840","8.160","90.50","14","15.00"],["","","02 B 65M","0.411"